<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17485" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fā^brīlis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		faber, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to an artificer</i>
			(class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scalprum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					27, 49, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opera ad fabrilia surgere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 415</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dextra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 175</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vincula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Am. 1, 9, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gluten,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 8,
					7</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glutinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 11, 49, § 182</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fumus gratiam affert vinis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					14, 1, 3, § 16</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hence, uva,</span>”
				i. e. <i>smoke-dried</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Tard. 4, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ben. 6, 38</span></i>
			: erratum, <i>of the sculptor</i> or <i>artist</i>, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				6, 1, 17</span></i>.—In the <i>neutr.
			subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fabrīlĭa</span></b> , ium, <i>mechanical tools</i> or <i>implements</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tractant fabrilia fabri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 1, 116</span></i>
			.—* <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fā^brīlĭter</span></b> , <i>skilfully</i>, <i>in a workmanlike
				manner</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opifex fabriliter aptans Composuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Apoth. 583</span></i>
			.</div>
